      "message": "Storing the expiry inside authorized_keys has a problem with backwards compatibility. When the keys have \u0027# EXPIRES\u0027 and if the gerrit version is rolled back to a point that does not have this new logic, those \u0027valid\u0027 keys will now be ignored. Would it be better to instead add a new separate file where we store expirations and not change the format of authorized_keys, i.e add authorized_keys.config (similar to the existing tokens.config)?\n\nFor example:\n```\n[key \"foo\"]\n\texpiration \u003d 2026-11-16T00:00:00Z\n[key \"bar\"]\n\texpiration \u003d 2030-01-02T03:04:05Z\n```",
